      "content": "8.1 Ancient India"
    },
    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "Ancient India spans major phases including the Indus Valley Civilization (3300–1300 BCE), the Vedic Age, and the Maurya Empire (322–185 BCE).",
        "Medieval India is primarily marked by the reigns of the Delhi Sultanate (1206–1526 CE) and the Mughal Empire (1526–1857 CE).",
        "Modern India focuses on significant historical events following the decline of the Mughal Empire."
      ],
